# RONDB-1062: a proactively detected deadlock is surfaced as
# ER_LOCK_DEADLOCK (1213), with extra detail in SHOW WARNINGS.
# con1 holds row 1 and wants row 2; con2 holds row 2 and wants row 1, a
# true 2-cycle on table t1.  Exactly one transaction is aborted with 1213;
# on that connection SHOW WARNINGS carries the "Deadlock detected by NDB"
# detail line - the victim operation's table name and the contended table
# id (masked below as it is not stable across runs).
# SHOW WARNINGS on the victim connection (contended table id masked).  It
# carries the standard temporary-error warning, the RONDB-1062 deadlock
# detail, the 1213 deadlock error, and the NDB transaction rollback
# diagnostic.  (SHOW WARNINGS does not clear the diagnostics area, so the
# victim's warnings are still present here.)
Level	Code	Message
Warning	1297	Got temporary error 266 'Time-out in NDB, probably caused by deadlock' from NDB
Warning	1297	Got temporary error 266 'Deadlock detected by NDB; victim operation on table 't1'; table involved (id): #' from NDB
Error	1213	Deadlock found when trying to get lock; try restarting transaction
Error	1622	Storage engine NDB does not support rollback for this statement. Transaction rolled back and must be restarted
